1. Containers With Most Water:

Code:
class Solution {
    public int maxArea(int[] height) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = height.length - 1;

        int maxWater = 0;

        while (left < right) {

            int width = right - left;
            int currentHeight = Math.min(height[left], height[right]);

            int currentArea = width * currentHeight;

            maxWater = Math.max(maxWater, currentArea);

            // Move the pointer with the smaller height
            if (height[left] < height[right]) {
                left++;
            } else {
                right--;
            }
        }

        return maxWater;
    }
}

Approach:
Use the two-pointer technique with pointers at both ends. Calculate the area using the smaller height, update the maximum area, then move the pointer with the smaller height inward to potentially find a larger area.

Complexity:
Time: O(n) — each pointer moves toward the other at most once.
Space: O(1) — only a few variables are used.

